  "notes": "Announced by Satya Nadella in the Microsoft Ignite 2023 opening keynote on 2023-11-15 and released with the Microsoft Research blog post of 2023-12-12, which says it is in the Azure AI Studio model catalog. The keynote calls it open source and says it will come to the catalog and models as a service; the card now states the MIT license (commit history shows the LICENSE file was updated on 2024-02-06). Base model, neither RLHF-aligned nor instruction-tuned. Hugging Face repo created 2023-12-13 (API, not a stated date). Azure AI Studio catalog access is not recorded as api because the sources do not describe a hosted endpoint at release."
